  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc 0.7250). Evidence shows scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer is the strongest backbone, but the image encoder and fusion strategy still have unresolved trade-offs: resnet50 achieved lower accuracy (0.7131) yet notably higher F1 (0.6945 vs 0.6847) than imagenet_vit_l, suggesting it captures complementary features that a different fusion strategy might exploit. config_011 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the only untested combination that pairs the F1-strong resnet50 encoder with concat fusion while retaining the proven transformer aggregation. This tests whether the resnet50–RNA interaction benefits from a different fusion mechanism, potentially unlocking an accuracy gain over the current best. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, testing this high-potential variant is the best balance of exploiting the known strong backbone and exploring the one remaining untested pairing within it."
}

